# Infinite-Free-Coding-Rotation-Strategy

# 🔄 24-Hour AI Coding "Infinite Rotation" Strategy
## Continuous Development Without Running Out of Free Quotas (2026 Edition)

This repository outlines a tactical rotation of terminal-based AI agents to maintain a 100% development uptime using only free-tier quotas and open-source tools.

---

### 🧰 The Modern CLI Stack

| Tool | Core Strength | Free Tier Mechanism |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| [**Antigravity CLI**](https://antigravity.google) | Agentic Orchestration | Multi-agent rolling session blocks |
| [**OpenCode**](https://github.com) | Terminal-First Workflow | Unlimited with [Ollama](https://ollama.com) / Local LLMs |
| [**Aider**](https://aider.chat) | Git-Native Editing | Free software; pair with free API keys |
| [**Freebuff**](https://freebuff.com) | High-Tier Model Access | 6 one-hour free sessions per day |
| [**Kilo CLI**](https://kilo.ai/articles/best-cli-coding-agents) | Platform Flexibility | Most model-agnostic free connection tier |
| [**GitHub Copilot CLI**](https://github.com) | IDE/Terminal Context | 2,000 monthly completions / 50 chats |

---

### ⏰ The 24-Hour Execution Roadmap

To maintain a continuous workflow, rotate through these tools based on their specific quota reset windows:

#### Phase 1: High-Energy Architecture (08:00 - 13:00)
*   **Tool:** [**Antigravity CLI**](https://antigravity.google)
*   **Strategy:** Start the day with Google's official successor to Gemini CLI. It features async multi-agent orchestration.
*   **Best For:** Scaffolding new features and complex architectural planning that requires multiple agents working in parallel.

#### Phase 2: Logic Implementation & Refactoring (13:00 - 18:00)
*   **Tool:** [**Kilo CLI**](https://kilo.ai/articles/best-cli-coding-agents) or [**Aider**](https://aider.chat)
*   **Strategy:** Switch to Kilo for deep feature building. Kilo is noted as the most model-flexible option in 2026. 
*   **Workflow:** Use Aider for surgical, git-native code edits that need a clean audit trail. Pair these with free API tiers from providers like Qwen (which offers 2,000 requests/day).

#### Phase 3: The Evening Sprint (18:00 - 23:00)
*   **Tool:** [**Freebuff**](https://freebuff.com)
*   **Strategy:** Activate your **6 daily one-hour sessions**. 
*   **Tip:** Use these sessions for intense bursts of coding that require high-tier reasoning models without using up your API credits.

#### Phase 4: Overnight "Infinite" Mode (23:00 - 08:00)
*   **Tool:** [**OpenCode**](https://github.com) + [**Ollama**](https://ollama.com)
*   **Strategy:** Run [DeepSeek](https://deepseek.com) or [Llama-](https://meta.com) models locally on your hardware.
*   **Benefit:** This is **mathematically infinite**. Since it runs locally, you face zero rate limits and zero cost. Use this for writing tests, documentation, and routine cleanup.

---

### 🛠️ Optimization Tactics

*   **Context Bridging:** Before rotating tools, use your current agent to generate a `STATE.md` file. Pipe this into the next tool so it resumes instantly without wasting tokens on "re-learning" your project.
*   **Git-First Workflow:** Use [Aider](https://aider.chat) for every AI edit to ensure every change becomes a reviewable commit, making it easy to undo mistakes across any tool in the rotation.
*   **Local MCP Servers:** Use [Jan](https://jan.ai) to host local Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers, allowing cloud-based CLI agents to read your local files without hitting heavy API context limits.

